{"id":27915,"slug":"thirty-two-short-films-about-glenn-gould","title":"Thirty Two Short Films About Glenn Gould","year":1993,"country":"Canada","duration":93,"spine":1268,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/27915-thirty-two-short-films-about-glenn-gould","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/62bbfbf0c2233d9caee286285f4af79e/2N5DrBiNrrT1TfNAQDgCxLZDGADWpG_large.jpg","description":"A rare film biography as boldly unconventional as its subject, writer-director François Girard’s visionary portrait of iconoclastic, world-renowned pianist Glenn Gould explodes the conventions of the form to illuminate the brilliant mind and innermost obsessions of a singular artist. Across thirty-two vignettes encompassing everything from dramatic sketches to documentary interviews to avant-garde animation, Thirty Two Short Films About Glenn Gould pieces together the story of Gould’s trajectory from child prodigy to celebrated concert pianist who turned his back on public performance to pursue his all-consuming fascination with recording technology. Led by a tour-de-force performance by Colm Feore and underscored by Gould’s landmark recordings of Bach’s Goldberg Variations, Girard’s film daringly deconstructs the enigma of genius.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"François Girard","slug":"francois-girard"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Colm Feore","role":"Glenn Gould","slug":"colm-feore"},{"actor":"Derek Keurvorst","role":"Gould’s father","slug":"derek-keurvorst"},{"actor":"Katya Ladan","role":"Gould’s mother","slug":"katya-ladan"},{"actor":"Devon Anderson","role":"Young Glenn, age three","slug":"devon-anderson"},{"actor":"Joshua Greenblatt","role":"Young Glenn, age eight","slug":"joshua-greenblatt"},{"actor":"Sean Ryan","role":"Young Glenn, age twelve","slug":"sean-ryan"},{"actor":"Kate Hennig","role":"Chambermaid","slug":"kate-hennig"},{"actor":"Sharon Bernbaum","role":"Female guide","slug":"sharon-bernbaum"},{"actor":"Don McKellar","role":"Concert promoter","s